splashsurf is a command-line tool to reconstruct surface meshes from
particle data, typically from SPH (smoothed particle hydrodynamics)
fluid simulations. It computes a level set of the SPH density field on
a sparse grid and extracts a triangle mesh with marching cubes, with
optional smoothing, decimation and normal computation. Input formats
include VTK, BGEO, PLY, XYZ and JSON; output formats include VTK, PLY
and OBJ. The reconstruction is parallelized with rayon.
